<title>UK: Millennium &amp; Copthorne buys French hotel.</title>
<headline>Millennium &amp; Copthorne buys French hotel.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Millennium &amp; Copthorne Hotels said on Monday it had purchased the freehold of the Copthorne Commodore Hotel in Paris from Ugitour, a subsidiary of French insurance firm Union des Assurance de Paris (UAP).</p>
<p>Millennium had purchased the freehold for 125 million francs, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Millennium, which previously held a leasehold interest in the hotel, said it planned to refurbish it extensively next year.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
